===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*men- (stand out)}}
First attested ''ante'' 1300: borrowed from the {{bor|en|fro|manace}}, {{m|fro|menace}}, from the {{der|en|VL.|*minācia}}, from {{m|la|minax|mināx, mināciae|threatening; threats}}, from {{m|la|minor||I threaten}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[perceived]] [[threat]] or [[danger]].
#* {{RQ:Dryden Aeneis|9}}
#*: the dark '''menace''' of the distant war.
# The act of [[threatening]].
# {{lb|en|informal}} An [[annoying]] and [[bothersome]] person or thing.

